# Checking-account rules for checking.csv — the CORRECT match.
#
# Everything a well-formed candidate has: a date-format that reads this file's
# dates, a fields list as wide as the file, a `currency` so amounts land in $
# rather than in the bare commodity, and an if-rule for every description in the
# data so no posting falls through to `expenses:unknown`.

skip 1
fields date, description, amount-out, amount-in
date-format %m/%d/%Y
currency $

account1 assets:bank:checking
account2 expenses:unknown

if ACME PAYROLL
    account2 income:salary

if
COFFEE
STARBUCKS
PEETS
    account2 expenses:food:coffee

if LANDLORD LLC
    account2 expenses:home:rent

if HARDWARE STORE
    account2 expenses:home:supplies
